      "description": "<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">This category features Urdu novels centered on secret agents, spies, and intelligence officers — often with a possessive hero whose profession keeps him emotionally distant until the heroine breaks through his guard. Some novels in this collection also flip the trope, giving readers a heroine working as a secret agent herself, which adds a different kind of tension to the romance.</p><p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\"><strong>Rag e Jaan Hai Wo by Ana Ilyas</strong> follows this intense, possessive-hero pattern common in spy-based fiction. <strong>Aisi Ki Tesi by Ramsha Hussain</strong> rounds out the collection with its own take on intelligence-based romance, where suspense and personal relationships constantly collide.</p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">For readers who like their love stories layered with secrecy, danger, and a hero (or heroine) leading a double life, this is the right category to explore. All novels are free to read online or download as PDF, with new titles added regularly.</p>",
