      "_id": {
        "$numberInt": "28"
      },
      "name": "After Marriage",
      "slug": "after-marriage",
      "description": "<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">This category is for readers who prefer their romance to unfold after the wedding, not before it — Urdu novels where the main characters are husband and wife from the very first chapter.</p><p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\"><strong>Dastaan e Junoon by Haaley Noor</strong> and <strong>Ankaboot by Noor Rajput</strong> both explore this theme, with couples starting off distant or unfamiliar with each other and gradually finding common ground as their marriage progresses. For readers who enjoy a slightly intense, possessive dynamic within a married relationship, <strong>My Possessive Mafia by Barbie Boo</strong> is also part of this collection.</p><p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">Two more notable additions here are <strong>Teri Ulfat Mein Sanam by Meem Ain</strong> and <strong>Tu Mile Mil Jaye Rahat by Maryam Rajpoot</strong> — both following the emotional journey of couples adjusting to married life while love slowly develops between them.</p><p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">Browse this section for Urdu novels focused on post-marriage romance and relationships that grow with time. All titles are free to read online or download as PDF.</p>",
