      "name": "Cousin Marriage",
      "slug": "cousin-marriage",
      "description": "<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">Cousin marriage novels are a genre deeply tied to South Asian family culture, where marriages within the extended family — often decided by elders — bring their own mix of romance, tension, and sometimes revenge. A recurring trope in this space is the rude cousin hero, someone who resents the arrangement at first but slowly softens as the story progresses within a joint family setting.</p><p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\"><strong>Meri Bachpan Ki Mohabbat by Rahim Rahi</strong> captures the childhood-to-marriage journey common in cousin-based stories, while <strong>Anokha Nikah by Zahra Jaffery</strong> explores a forced cousin marriage that unfolds into something unexpected. <strong>Noor e Mohabbat by Rimsha Hussain</strong> adds an age difference element, a common twist in this genre where one cousin is noticeably older or more mature.</p><p>\r\n\r\n</p><p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">If you enjoy Urdu novels rooted in joint family dynamics, forced cousin marriages, and hero characters who start off cold but change over time, this collection is exactly that. All titles are free to read online or download as PDF.</p>",
