      },
      "name": "Forced Marriage",
      "slug": "forced-marriage",
      "description": "<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">Forced marriage novels are one of the most popular genres in Urdu fiction, built around a nikah that neither the hero nor heroine actually chose — whether due to family pressure, a sudden decision, or circumstances beyond their control. The story then follows how two unwilling partners slowly move from resentment or resistance to genuine love.</p><p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\"><strong>Chaal by Yaman Eva</strong> follows this theme closely, with a marriage forced by circumstances that neither lead was prepared for. <strong>Professor Khan by Zanoor Writes</strong> adds an age difference angle, a common pairing in forced marriage stories where one partner is noticeably more mature or established than the other. <strong>Sanson Mein Bas Tum by Zahra Fatima</strong> also explores this dynamic, following a couple navigating an unwanted marriage that gradually turns into something real.</p><p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">If you enjoy Urdu novels where love isn't a choice at first but grows despite it, along with themes of revenge, family conflict, and slow emotional change, this collection is written around exactly that. All titles are free to read online or download as PDF.</p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><hr class=\"border-border-200 border-t-0.5 my-3 mx-1.5\">",
