      "writer_id": {
        "$numberInt": "8"
      },
      "series_id": null,
      "season_number": null,
      "description": "<p>Hum Deewane Se is a romantic family drama that beautifully captures the emotions of childhood commitment and delayed love. Written by Biya Ahmed, this novel is perfect for readers who enjoy stories built around cousin marriage, joint family setups, and a hero who hides his love behind a tough exterior.</p><h2><strong>Story Summary</strong></h2><p>The story begins when Kamal Fayyaz, the family elder, arranges the Nikah of his 8-year-old grandson Raham Hassan with his 1-year-old granddaughter Heer Inam, hoping to secure the family's future. As Heer grows up, she proudly calls herself Raham's \"childhood wife,\" but deep down she feels neglected. Raham never expresses love the way she expects — no gifts, no sweet words — so she sees him only as a strict and grumpy man.</p><p>In reality, Raham, now a 28-year-old businessman, loves Heer deeply. He keeps his distance on purpose, wanting her to focus on her studies before starting married life. Everything changes when Heer overhears a phone call between Raham and a woman named Naema. Not knowing that Raham is only helping his friend Fowad solve a marital problem, Heer assumes he is planning a second marriage. Hurt and angry, she storms into his office and introduces herself to his staff as his childhood wife.</p><p>The misunderstanding is later resolved by Raham's aunt, Faiza, who explains to him that Heer simply wants to feel loved the traditional way. Realizing this, Raham plans a beautiful Rukhsati on Eid night — decorating the rooftop with lights, surprising her with chocolates, flowers, and a bracelet, and finally confessing his true feelings. The novel ends on a warm, emotional note as Heer finally understands the depth of her husband's love.</p><h2><strong>Main Characters</strong></h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Raham Hassan</strong> – A serious, responsible businessman who hides his love to protect Heer's future.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Heer Inam</strong> – A lively, emotional girl who dreams of a fairy-tale romance with her childhood groom.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Rida Hassan</strong> – Raham's sister and Heer's close friend, who often defends her brother.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Faiza (Phupho)</strong> – The wise aunt who helps clear misunderstandings between the couple.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Zarina &amp; Khadija</strong> – The supportive mothers who wish to see the couple happily united.</li>\r\n</ul><h2><strong>Why Readers Love This Novel</strong></h2><p><!--StartFragment-->\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--EndFragment--></p><p>Hum Deewane Se stands out for its mix of innocence and emotion. It combines popular romance themes like childhood Nikah, cousin marriage, age gap, and a joint family background, along with a rude-but-caring hero — a combination that keeps readers hooked till the last page.</p>",
