      "description": "<p>Dastan-e-Hayat by Zohra Bint-e-Khalid is available to read online and download in PDF on our website. Enjoy this emotional Urdu novel with easy online reading or offline PDF access.</p><h2><strong>Main Characters</strong></h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Hayat Shahir Baloch:</strong> A talented and passionate debater with a fiery temper, sharp intellect, and a strong will, who matures into a composed young woman and later pursues law.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ayan Iftikhar Mir:</strong> Hayat's cousin and eventual husband, a patriotic young man who leaves the family business to join the Army, rising to the rank of Captain/Major.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Umer Shahir Baloch:</strong> Hayat's elder brother, who takes over his father's business in Bahrain after completing his studies.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Laraib Muzammil:</strong> Hayat's closest friend and a brilliant student who later studies law alongside her and marries Ayan's friend, Hazig.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Hazig Nawaz Mir:</strong> Ayan's best friend and cousin, known for his humor and mischievous nature.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ayat Iftikhar Mir:</strong> Ayan's younger sister and Hayat's cousin, a loyal and warm-hearted girl.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Shahir Baloch:</strong> Hayat's father, a loving parent entangled in a bitter family rivalry with his brother Tariq.</li>\r\n</ul><h3><strong>Story Summary</strong></h3><p>Dastan-e-Hayat opens with the lively bond between Hayat and her family, marked by constant playful rivalry with her cousin Ayan, as the two trade nicknames and banter. When Ayan decides to join the Army against his family's business plans, his father agrees on the condition that he marry a girl of his choosing — unaware to Ayan, it is Hayat herself, whom he has secretly come to love.</p><p>Meanwhile, a long-standing feud between Hayat's father and his brother Tariq puts Hayat in danger, prompting the two fathers to quietly arrange Hayat and Ayan's marriage to protect her. Hayat agrees only out of respect for her father. Tragedy strikes just days later when both fathers are killed in an orchestrated attack. Suspecting his uncle Tariq's involvement but lacking proof, Ayan conceals the truth from Hayat to shield her fragile emotional state, distancing himself from her for four years.</p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; letter-spacing: 0.1px;\">Read Online or Download PDF</strong></p><p><!--StartFragment-->\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--EndFragment--></p><p>You can read the complete Dastan-e-Hayat novel online on our website or download the PDF to enjoy this memorable Urdu novel anytime, anywhere.</p>",
