      "description": "<h2><strong>Daastan e Firaq novel by Halima Saadia is available to read online easily and also download PDF free at Kitab Nagri.</strong></h2><p>Daastan e Firaq is an emotional romantic tragedy that explores love, family pride, and the painful consequences of forced decisions. Written by Halima Saadia, this novel is for readers who enjoy deep, heart-touching stories with a bittersweet, tragic ending rather than a typical happy one.</p><h2><strong>Story Summary</strong></h2><p>The story follows Shafaq Hayat, a simple and innocent university student, whose life changes when Shehryar Shah Bukhari, an Oxford-educated assistant professor, joins her university. What starts as a strict, formal relationship slowly turns into a deep bond during a university trip to Lake Saiful Muluk, and the two eventually fall in love. Shehryar soon confesses his feelings and proposes marriage.</p><p>However, Shafaq's cousin Irtiza Hayat has silently loved her for years. His father convinces Shafaq's parents to fix her Nikah with Irtiza without her consent, and when Shehryar's family comes with a proposal, Shafaq's father rejects them outright to honor the cousin marriage.</p><p>Heartbroken, Shafaq begs Irtiza to call off the wedding. Touched by her pain, Irtiza tries to convince his father too — but Shafaq's father refuses to change his decision, going to extreme lengths to force her agreement. Left with no choice, Shafaq gives in to save her family's honor.</p><p>When Shehryar comes to plead for Shafaq one last time, the situation turns violent, leading to a tragic confrontation that changes everything. Unable to bear the loss and the forced marriage ahead, Shafaq takes her own life the night before her wedding. Irtiza, shattered by the loss of both, leaves Pakistan forever, while the novel closes with a heartbreaking, unforgettable ending.</p><h2><strong>Main Characters</strong></h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Shafaq Hayat</strong> – An innocent, loving girl caught between true love and family obligations.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Shehryar Shah Bukhari</strong> – An intelligent, Oxford-returned professor who finds love but faces a tragic fate.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Irtiza Hayat</strong> – Shafaq's selfless cousin who sacrifices his own happiness for her.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Shahsawar Hayat</strong> – Shafaq's father, representing rigid family pride and pressure.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Sufiyan Hayat</strong> – Shafaq's elder brother, driven by ego and family honor.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Phuppo Janat</strong> – The paternal aunt who offers emotional support through the darkest moments.</li>\r\n</ul><h2><strong>Why Readers Love This Novel</strong></h2><p><!--StartFragment-->\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--EndFragment--></p><p>Daastan e Firaq is not a typical love story — it's a powerful tragedy about how family pride and forced decisions can destroy innocent lives. With its themes of sacrifice, cousin marriage, and forced Nikah, this novel leaves a lasting emotional impact on its readers.</p>",
