      "season_number": null,
      "description": "<p>Rab Se Jurne Ka Safar by Umm e Huraira is an emotional Islamic novel about a girl's journey from sin to repentance, her struggle to embrace the veil, and her patience through a terminal illness. Read online or download PDF.</p><h2><strong>Main Characters</strong></h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Fatima:</strong> A university student from a rich family. After a wrong relationship with a guy named Sufiyan leaves her restless, she turns to religion, starts wearing a niqab, faces harsh opposition from her family, and later battles liver cancer with great patience.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Qurat-ul-Ain (Ainee):</strong> Fatima's classmate who wears a full black veil and has deep Islamic knowledge. She guides Fatima toward repentance and later marries Shahryar in a simple wedding.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Shahryar:</strong> A hardworking guy who runs a bookstore. Under his friend Maaz's influence, he leaves music and smoking behind, refuses to take dowry, and marries Qurat-ul-Ain purely because of her faith and character.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Maaz:</strong> Qurat-ul-Ain's religious brother who mentors Shahryar. After his mother's death, he leaves to serve the Muslim community elsewhere.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Zonisha:</strong> A modern doctor who marries Fatima's brother Haider. She's deeply moved by Fatima's transformation and eventually starts wearing the veil too.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Mrs Rayan:</strong> Fatima's mother, who first opposes her daughter's religious change but later softens after a scary dream and seeing Fatima's sincere prayers at night.</li>\r\n</ul><h2><strong>Story Summary</strong></h2><p>Fatima gets caught up in a wrong relationship with Sufiyan, which leaves her mentally disturbed. Looking for peace, she turns to her classmate Qurat-ul-Ain, who introduces her to the Quran and prayer. When she ends things with Sufiyan, he takes revenge by sending edited pictures of her to her family. Fatima faces harsh treatment from her mother and brother but bears it all patiently, following Qurat-ul-Ain's advice on \"beautiful patience.\"</p><p>When Fatima starts wearing full niqab, her family strongly opposes her — calling her names and even locking her in her room. But she stays firm, and eventually her patience and prayers soften her mother's heart. Meanwhile, Shahryar completely changes his life under Maaz's guidance and marries Qurat-ul-Ain in a simple, dowry-free wedding based only on her faith.</p><p>Later, Fatima is diagnosed with advanced liver cancer. She goes to Canada for treatment and, despite immense pain, spends her final days spreading Islamic teachings to non-Muslims there. Her sincerity even leads a nurse and a family to accept Islam. She eventually passes away peacefully while reciting the Kalima, and her example inspires her sister-in-law Zonisha to start wearing the veil too.</p><h2><strong style=\"letter-spacing: 0.1px;\">Read Online or Download PDF</strong></h2><p><!--StartFragment-->\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--EndFragment--></p><p>You can read the complete Rab Se Jurne Ka Safar novel online or download the PDF anytime from our website.</p>",
