      "series_id": null,
      "season_number": null,
      "description": "<!--EndFragment--><p><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); letter-spacing: 0.1px;\">Read</span><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); letter-spacing: 0.1px;\">&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>Lams-e-Junoon by Zoya Ali Shah online or download the PDF: a forced marriage romance of Rumaan and Meerab, and Shahmir and Mirha, full of revenge, love, and redemption.&nbsp;</p><!--StartFragment--><!--EndFragment--><h2><strong>Main Characters</strong></h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Rumaan Shah (Romeo):</strong> A successful, proud, short-tempered businessman carrying a bitter past after being betrayed by his cousin, Mahek.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Meerab Malik:</strong> The stubborn, spoiled only daughter of businessman Malik Zubair, who falls hard for Rumaan at first sight.</li>\r\n<li><strong>ACP Shahmir Malik:</strong> Meerab's protective older brother, a brave and respected police officer.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Mirha:</strong> Rumaan's innocent, shy younger sister, whom he has sheltered fiercely from the world.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Mahek:</strong> Rumaan's cousin and past love, who once rejected him for money and status.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Dr. Shahzeb:</strong> Rumaan's childhood friend and a heart surgeon, secretly in love with Mirha.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ahmer:</strong> Rumaan's other loyal friend, recovering from drug addiction with his friends' support.</li>\r\n</ul><h2><strong>Story Summary</strong></h2><p>Meerab falls for the arrogant Rumaan Shah after meeting him at a mall, but scarred by his cousin's betrayal, he cruelly rejects her, pushing her to attempt suicide. When her brother, ACP Shahmir, learns Rumaan's rejection nearly cost his sister her life, he forces Rumaan into marrying Meerab by threatening him through his sheltered sister, Mirha. Shahmir then also forces the terrified Mirha into marrying him.</p><p>After marriage, Rumaan treats Meerab with cruelty out of anger, even leaving her out in a freezing storm — but caring for her when she falls dangerously ill melts his heart, and he eventually falls deeply in love with her. Meanwhile, Shahmir turns out to be incredibly gentle and loving toward Mirha, helping her overcome her fears and win her heart completely.</p><p><!--StartFragment-->\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--EndFragment--></p><p>A dark figure from Mirha's past resurfaces at her wedding, triggering a breakdown, and Shahmir and Rumaan track him down for justice. Meanwhile, Rumaan's corrupt relatives lose everything, and he buys back his family's old haveli. He rejects Mahek for good and marries her off to his friend Ahmer. The story ends happily with both couples finding peace, and Meerab and Rumaan expecting their first child.</p>",
