      "series_id": null,
      "season_number": null,
      "description": "<p>Ghasiq by Mahira Zaynab Khan: a haveli-based saga of secret identities, forbidden love, a hidden gangster don, and a Jinn's forbidden devotion. Read online or download PDF.</p><h2><strong>Main Characters</strong></h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Abeer Ghazi:</strong> The eldest grandson of Saadat Ghazi and CEO of Ghazi Industries. Seen by everyone as the ideal grandson, he's secretly a powerful gangster running an international smuggling network — and he's in love with his cousin Resham.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Resham Zamir Ghazi:</strong> Saadat Ghazi's granddaughter, an MBA student who falls in love with a humble servant named \"Yusuf,\" later discovering his real identity.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Anas Ghazi / Yusuf:</strong> The son of Saadat's estranged stepson, a DSP. He enters the mansion undercover as a servant to expose Abeer's criminal empire and reclaim his family identity, all while falling for Resham.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Bareeze Ghazi:</strong> A blunt, outspoken granddaughter whose life changes when a righteous Jinn named Fatim becomes drawn to her and starts protecting her from dark forces.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Aashir Mirza:</strong> Saadat's grandson and a bike racer. He acts cold toward Bareeze but secretly loves her and plots to marry her to keep her safe.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Salar Ghazi:</strong> Abeer's younger brother, who runs a family business branch and later takes over the mansion. He's involved with his secretary, Mehr Mah.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Mehr Mah Sultan:</strong> Salar's secretary, from a family facing financial hardship.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Fatim:</strong> A righteous Jinn who protects Bareeze and falls for her.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Dariyan Durrani:</strong> A mysterious young man tied to spiritual matters and Jinn gatherings.</li>\r\n</ul><h2><strong>Story Summary</strong></h2><p>The story is set in the grand Saadeen Haveli, ruled by patriarch Saadat Ghazi, whose golden grandson Abeer is admired by all — but is secretly leading a double life as a criminal mastermind.</p><p>A quiet servant named Yusuf turns out to be Anas Ghazi, working undercover to expose Abeer's crimes. Resham falls in love with him without knowing his real identity, and when her family arranges her marriage to Salar, Anas stages a dramatic gunpoint marriage to claim her as his own.</p><p>Meanwhile, Bareeze wanders into a haunted floor of a friend's haveli and is saved by a Jinn named Fatim, who falls for her. Her family dismisses it as stress, but Aashir — who has secretly loved her for years — engineers a plan to break her engagement and marry her himself, becoming her protector.</p><p><!--StartFragment-->\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<!--EndFragment--></p><p>The biggest twist comes when Abeer's criminal identity is exposed after he orders the murder of Anas's parents. Anas eventually reveals the truth to the rest of the family, and Abeer flees the country as his empire collapses. Back at the haveli, Salar takes charge, and the surviving couples try to find peace in their new marriages — while Fatim, realizing a human-Jinn bond can never truly last, disappears from Bareeze's life forever.</p><h2><strong>Read Online or Download PDF</strong></h2><p><!--StartFragment-->\r\n<!--EndFragment--></p><p>You can read the complete Ghasiq novel online or download the PDF anytime from our website.</p>",
