      "season_number": null,
      "description": "<p>Read the complete Main Hari Piya novel online or download the PDF anytime from our website.<!--EndFragment--></p><h2><strong>Main Characters</strong></h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Hurrah:</strong> The heroine, who faces immense hardships and family cruelty yet remains patient and dignified throughout.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Sardar Abbas Hamdani:</strong> The hero, a righteous, well-educated lawyer and feudal leader who stands against cruel customs to protect his wife.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Noreen / Noore:</strong> Abbas's cousin, engaged to him since childhood, who later accepts a different destiny.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Aaliyan &amp; Ahmad:</strong> Abbas's loyal friends who support him through his struggles.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Dua:</strong> Hurrah and Abbas's beloved daughter.</li>\r\n</ul><h3><strong>Story Summary</strong></h3><p>The story opens with tragedy when Sardar Abbas's sister is murdered, and under the cruel tribal custom of Vanni, the innocent Hurrah is forcibly married to Abbas as blood compensation. Unlike a typical ruthless feudal lord, Abbas — an educated, principled lawyer — refuses to treat Hurrah as a punishment and vows to give her the respect and love she deserves as his lawful wife.</p><p>Despite his efforts, Hurrah suffers abuse and conspiracies at the hands of Abbas's mother and aunt, who want him to marry his childhood fiancée instead. Framed and endangered, Hurrah eventually flees with her daughter to protect herself. Abbas searches for her relentlessly while uncovering the real truth behind his sister's murder — a betrayal from someone he trusted.</p><p>In the end, Abbas reunites with Hurrah and their daughter, brings them home with full honor, and as the new village leader, bans the practice of Vanni for good.</p>",
