      "description": "<!--EndFragment--><p><span style=\"color: rgb(255, 255, 255); letter-spacing: 0.1px;\">Read the complete Junoon e Wafa novel online or download the PDF anytime from our website.</span></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 2rem; letter-spacing: 0.1px;\">Main Characters</strong></p><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Dameer Khan Afridi:</strong> The elder son of Asadullah Khan, a successful businessman running the family business abroad.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Zarbacht Rameez Khan:</strong> Dameer's cousin, a simple and innocent 17-year-old living in poverty with her ailing mother.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Daeer Khan Afridi:</strong> Dameer's younger brother, lively and romantic, deeply in love with his cousin Mehru.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Mehru-un-Nisa Khan:</strong> Daeer's cousin and university fellow, who becomes his wife.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Raim Khan Barkazai:</strong> Mehru's dignified elder brother, who falls one-sidedly in love with Anzish.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Anzish Buzdar:</strong> An independent, proud businesswoman managing her father's corporate projects.</li>\r\n</ul><h2><strong>Story Summary</strong></h2><p>The novel weaves together three love stories within one family. Daeer and Mehru marry despite old tribal tensions, but their happiness is threatened when a vengeful cousin abducts Mehru — until Daeer tracks him down and rescues her.</p><p>Meanwhile, Dameer returns home and discovers his impoverished aunt and her daughter Zarbacht, whom he's secretly cared for since childhood. When Zarbacht is nearly forced into an unequal marriage to fund her mother's cancer treatment, Dameer steps in, marries her himself, and becomes her pillar of support through her grief.</p><p>The third story follows Raim, who quietly loves Anzish, a proud businesswoman still hung up on Dameer. When she's attacked by a land mafia, Raim risks his life to save her, and his sacrifice finally makes her see his devotion. He recovers, and the two are united.</p><p>Years later, the whole family lives happily together in their ancestral home, surrounded by the next generation.</p><p><br></p>",
