      "season_number": null,
      "description": "<p> Hisar-e-Mohabbat by Aan Fatima is available to read online and download in PDF on our website. Enjoy this heartwarming Urdu family-romance novel with easy online reading or offline PDF access.</p><h2>Main Characters</h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Dr Saim Khan:</strong> A 27-year-old disciplined doctor deeply devoted to his family, who later marries Ayat.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ayat Qureshi:</strong> A 21-year-old beautiful, expressive, and outspoken girl who marries Saim.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Azlan Shah:</strong> A 30-year-old serious, dignified, and successful businessman intensely in love with Muhram.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Muhram Khan:</strong> A gentle, innocent, and modest girl who becomes Azlan's wife.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Affan Shah:</strong> Azlan's younger brother, an energetic, humorous, and dramatic young man who falls for Ezza.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ezza Khan:</strong> Muhram's 20-year-old beautiful sister who frequently bickers with Affan and eventually marries him.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Moazzam (Moazz) Affandi:</strong> A career-minded senior professional who works with Pareeshay and later marries her.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Pareeshay Shah:</strong> Azlan's younger sister who works under Moazz and later marries him.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Hijab Khan:</strong> Muhram and Ezza's 18-year-old playful younger sister, close friends with Ayan, whom she later marries.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ayan Qureshi:</strong> Ayat's brother who returns from higher studies in the US and eventually marries Hijab.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Faiq Malik:</strong> Walid's son, a foreign-educated man who serves as the primary antagonist.</li>\r\n</ul><h2>Story Summary</h2><p>Hisar-e-Mohabbat follows the interconnected lives of three families — the Khans, the Shahs, and the Affandi Qureishis — as their children navigate love, betrayal, and healing. Muhram is set to marry Faiq, but on the day of the Nikaah, he falsely slanders her character; when the truth comes out, the alliance breaks and the Shah family steps in, offering their eldest son Azlan as a groom. Azlan's devotion slowly heals Muhram's past wounds, and the two build a happy life together.</p><p>Meanwhile, Ayat and Saim's playful rivalry turns to love after Saim rescues her from danger and later marries her to honour her father's dying wish. Ezza and Affan share a mocking, bantering bond that deepens after Affan protects her from an acid attack by the vengeful Faiq, leading to a heartfelt proposal. Pareeshay and Moazz's professional partnership blossoms into romance and marriage. In the end, Faiq meets a fatal end while fleeing justice, and all four couples find lasting happiness within the warmth of their joint family.</p>",
