      "series_id": null,
      "season_number": null,
      "description": "<p><!--StartFragment--><!--EndFragment--></p><p><b>Read Zanjeer online</b><span><span>&nbsp;</span>on our platform or click the button below to<span>&nbsp;</span></span><b>download the complete PDF version for free</b><span><span>&nbsp;</span>to read offline anytime.</span></p><h2><b>Main Characters</b></h2><p><!--StartFragment--><!--EndFragment--></p><ul><li><p><b>Saleha Kabir Butt:</b><span>&nbsp;</span>An ambitious, value-driven girl who values education and faith.</p></li><li><p><b>Wajdan Qureshi:</b><span>&nbsp;</span>A wealthy businessman whose gentle care wins Saleha’s heart.</p></li><li><p><b>Riffat Fatima:</b><span>&nbsp;</span>An innocent girl brought into the haveli as Wani.</p></li><li><p><b>Sharjeel Butt:</b><span>&nbsp;</span>A stoic haveli member who becomes Riffat’s ultimate protector.</p></li><li><p><b>Haider &amp; Wajeeha (Jia):</b><span>&nbsp;</span>The couple whose marriage triggers the Watta Satta arrangement.</p></li><li><p><b>Shah Ji (Basharat Hussain) &amp; Afshans Phipho:</b><span>&nbsp;</span>The lovers whose hidden sacrifice exposes past family cruelty.</p></li></ul><h2><b>Story Summary</b></h2><p>The plot centers around a strict, traditional haveli ruled by patriarchal norms that suppress women and deny them education:</p><ul><li><p><b>Saleha &amp; Wajdan:</b> Saleha, an ambitious girl who dreams of becoming a teacher, sees her hopes crushed when her grandfather bans female education. To marry his own love, Wajeeha, Saleha’s brother Haider forces a Watta Satta (exchange marriage), tying Saleha to Wajeeha’s brother, <b>Wajdan Qureshi</b>. Though devastated initially, Saleha discovers Wajdan is a gentle, supportive partner who encourages her education and secures her a teaching job, leading to a deep romantic union.</p></li><li><p><b>Riffat &amp; Sharjeel:</b> Riffat is brought to the haveli as Wani (blood money) for a past crime and forced to marry Sharjeel. Contrary to the family's cruel nature, Sharjeel stands by Riffat, protecting her honour and elevating her to his true wife.</p></li><li><p><b>The Haveli Secret:</b> A long-held family secret surfaces when the loyal servant Shah Ji is revealed to be Basharat Hussain—a man who spent his youth disguised as a servant just to be near Saleha’s mute aunt, Afshans.</p></li></ul><p>As old prejudices crumble and light replaces dark traditions, the characters break free from their chains to find justice, family healing, and lasting love.</p>",
