      "series_id": null,
      "season_number": null,
      "description": "<p>Read Jugnoo Mere Taqub Mein online on our platform or click the button below to download the complete PDF version for free to read offline anytime.</p><h3>Main Characters</h3><ul><li><p><b>Gul Lala (Gul):</b> A fierce, gold-medalist Chitrali girl from a Sardar family who dreams of playing Shandur polo.</p></li><li><p><b>Dr. Ubadah Selim:</b> A dedicated veterinary doctor from Lahore sent to treat the Sardar family's paralyzed polo horses.</p></li><li><p><b>Ghazaan Khan:</b> Gul's foreign-educated cousin nominated for tribal leadership who harbors hidden motives.</p></li><li><p><b>Ibtihaj Khan:</b> The hot-tempered son of the current Sardar who deeply resents Ghazaan's leadership title.</p></li></ul><h3>Story Summary</h3><p>Set in the picturesque Ayun Valley of Chitral, the story centers around tribal politics, dark motives, and a struggle for justice:</p><ul><li><p><b>The Poisoning Mystery:</b> Dr. Ubadah arrives at the Sardar Haveli to secretly treat six paralyzed polo horses before the Shandur festival. Investigating the falsified reports, she uncovers that the horses were systematically poisoned—not by the hot-headed Ibtihaj as suspected, but by the polished Ghazaan Khan to manipulate tribal inheritance.</p></li><li><p><b>The Past Unveiled:</b> Alongside the horse mystery, a tragic family secret comes to light. Gul discovers that her biological father was murdered eighteen years prior over a leadership dispute by Ghazaan’s father, Naeem, who framed it as a riding accident.</p></li><li><p><b>Climax &amp; Justice:</b> Armed with evidence, Ubadah leverages the truth to secure Gul's right to play in the male-dominated Shandur Polo Festival. Gul plays brilliantly to win her late father's horse, Rustam, while police arrive at the match to arrest Ghazaan and Naeem for their crimes.</p></li></ul><p><!--StartFragment--><!--EndFragment--></p><p>The novel concludes with the Sardar abolishing autocratic tribal rule in favor of modern law, while a peaceful marriage proposal promises a bright future for Gul Lala.</p>",
