      "description": "<p>Read Hum Deewane Se online on our platform or click the button below to download the complete PDF version for free to read offline anytime.</p><h2>Main Characters</h2><ul><li><p><b>Heer Inam:</b> A playful, stubborn, and romantic female protagonist who was married off as an infant.</p></li><li><p><b>Raahim Hasan:</b> A strict, responsible businessman holding a double master's degree, who is Heer's childhood husband.</p></li><li><p><b>Rida Hasan:</b> Raahim’s sister and Heer's same-age cousin and best friend.</p></li><li><p><b>Faiza Aatif:</b> Raahim and Heer’s affectionate aunt who acts as a mentor and mediator for the couple.</p></li><li><p><b>Mehran Somro:</b> Raahim’s village-born college friend who falls in love with and marries Rida.</p></li></ul><h2>Story Summary</h2><p>The narrative revolves around a traditional family-arranged childhood marriage and its evolving dynamics:</p><ul><li><p><b>The Childhood Union:</b> Heer and Raahim's <i>Nikah</i> was performed by their grandfather when Heer was just a year old, and Raahim was eight. Growing up under one joint-family roof, they develop contrasting personalities—Heer becomes playful and dramatic, while Raahim grows into a strict, disciplined businessman.</p></li><li><p><b>Post-Rukhsati Adjustments:</b> After a formal <i>Rukhsati</i>, Heer struggles with the realities of married life and views her husband as overly harsh. Their early marital days are filled with humorous clashes, petty arguments, and playful misunderstandings during family trips and daily tasks.</p></li><li><p><b>Maturity &amp; Romantic Realisation:</b> Guided by their wise aunt Faiza, Raahim gradually softens his strict demeanour to express his lifelong devotion. Realising that his strictness was merely a protective shell, Heer sheds her immature outlook and accepts him completely.</p></li><li><p><b>Parallel Arc:</b> Alongside the main couple, the novel traces a warm secondary love story between Heer's best friend Rida and Raahim's friend Mehran.</p></li></ul><p><!--StartFragment--><div><response-element><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><!----><elicitations></elicitations></response-element></div><!--EndFragment--></p><p>As old childhood bickerings give way to emotional maturity, the novel concludes as a heartfelt journey of forced childhood ties blossoming into genuine lifelong love.</p>",
