      "description": "<p><!--StartFragment--><!--EndFragment--></p><p><span>Read the complete Anmol Mohabbat novel online on our website or download the PDF to enjoy this beautiful Urdu novel anytime, anywhere.</span></p><h2>Main Characters</h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Minha Usman:</strong> The innocent, emotional, and sensitive female protagonist who struggles emotionally after her father's death and is closely protected by her mother and brother.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Umar Ibrahim:</strong> The brilliant, mature, and deeply caring male protagonist who takes on responsibility early in life and protects Minha from hardship.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ahad Ibrahim:</strong> Umar's younger, cheerful, and mischievous brother — also Minha's foster-milk brother, sharing a strong bond with both siblings.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Samina Usman:</strong> Minha's loving mother and Umar's long-lost paternal aunt.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ahsan Ibrahim:</strong> Umar and Ahad's father and Samina's brother, who carries years of regret over losing contact with his sister.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Rana Ahsan:</strong> Umar and Ahad's prideful and controlling mother, whose past actions caused the family separation.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Laila Iftikhar:</strong> A beautiful and wealthy classmate obsessively in love with Umar, who acts as the antagonist and tries to create misunderstandings out of jealousy.</li>\r\n</ul><h2>Story Summary</h2><p>Anmol Mohabbat follows Minha, an overprotected and sensitive girl deeply affected by her father's sudden death. Pushed by her mother to attend university, she struggles with anxiety and an injury on her very first days — until she's rescued by Umar Ibrahim, a mature senior student who is instantly captivated by her innocence.</p><p>As the story unfolds, it's revealed that Umar's father and Minha's mother are long-separated siblings, torn apart years ago by the schemes of Umar's mother, Rana. When Minha's mother falls critically ill and faces threats from greedy relatives, Umar steps in to protect her — and quickly arranges a Nikkah with Minha to shield her legally and socially. Their bond deepens further when it's discovered that Umar's brother Ahad is Minha's foster-milk brother, creating a pure and protective family connection.</p><p>Jealous rivals and family opposition threaten their happiness, and tragedy strikes when Umar is critically shot while saving his best friend, slipping into a coma. The crisis finally softens his mother's heart, reuniting the long-broken family. Umar recovers, and the novel ends joyfully with a wedding celebration, the birth of their daughter Haniya, and happiness for the rest of the family as well.</p>",
