      "season_number": null,
      "description": "<p><!--StartFragment--><div><div><div><div><div><div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div></div><div></div><!--EndFragment--></p><div><p><!--StartFragment--><!--EndFragment--></p><p><span>Read the complete Tere Ishq Ki Mujhko Aadat Hai novel online on our website or download the PDF to enjoy this powerful Urdu novel anytime, anywhere.</span></p><h2>Main Characters</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>Aslan Mir (Hero):</strong> A serious, commanding, and honour-bound landlord (jaageerdar) hardened by circumstance. He marries Aroosha to take revenge on Shahnawaz Khan, treating her harshly at first while secretly falling deeply in love with her.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Aroosha (Heroine):</strong> Shahnawaz Khan's daughter — strikingly beautiful, innocent, chatty, and a little carefree. She's terrified of Aslan's harsh behaviour at first but gradually falls in love with him.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Hania:</strong> Aslan's younger sister and Aroosha's best friend, who is in love with Hisham.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Hisham (Hashu):</strong> Aroosha's brother (technically her cousin), who truly loves Hania and is deeply protective of his sister.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Aaliyah / Aafia:</strong> Aslan's first wife (his cousin) — a selfish, beauty-obsessed woman who betrayed Aslan by conspiring with Shahnawaz Khan.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Shahnawaz Khan:</strong> Aroosha's father and Hisham's uncle/stepfather — a corrupt, self-serving man consumed by wealth and old rivalries.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Maan Ji (Shazia):</strong> Aslan's strict but caring mother, who eventually accepts Aroosha wholeheartedly.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Story Summary</h2>\r\n<p>Tere Ishq Ki Mujhko Aadat Hai is a tale of revenge, betrayal, and love that refuses to stay buried. Aslan Mir's marriage to his cousin Aaliyah ends in disgrace when she's caught in an affair with his enemy, Shahnawaz Khan, publicly humiliating him. Seeking revenge, Aslan storms into Shahnawaz's home on the day of Aroosha's forced wedding to someone else — and instead takes her for himself at gunpoint, marrying her to settle his score with her father.</p>\r\n<p>For the first six months, Aslan keeps Aroosha locked away in his mansion, treating her coldly as the daughter of his enemy. But her innocence and childlike nature slowly melt his hardened heart, and he falls completely in love with her. As deeper conspiracies unravel involving Aslan's own relatives, tragedy strikes when the family's enemies kill his grandmother and injure his mother, and attempt to harm Aroosha and Hisham as well.</p>\r\n<p>In a fierce final confrontation, Aslan and Hisham take down their enemies, while Shahnawaz Khan dies protecting his own daughter and Aaliyah meets her end as well. After enduring every hardship, Aslan and Aroosha's relationship blossoms into a joyful family life with three children, while Hania and Hisham also find their happy ending in marriage.</p></div>",
      "image": "images/146-6a79a650bc07f-tere-ishq-ki-mujhko-aadat-hai-novel-by-zohra-farakh-hassan-complete.webp",
