      "description": "<h2><p><!--StartFragment--><!--EndFragment--></p></h2><p><span>Read the complete Sitara-e-Zeest novel online on our website or download the PDF to enjoy this heartfelt Urdu novel anytime, anywhere.</span></p><h2>Main Characters</h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Arsa Hashim:</strong> The central female protagonist, a brilliant student who faces severe emotional distress and physical abuse from her father due to a misunderstanding orchestrated by her stepfamily.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Tqi:</strong> The male protagonist, Arsa's chemistry teacher from Islamabad, who marries her under difficult circumstances and later helps her overcome her trauma and low self-esteem.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Alishba:</strong> Arsa's best friend and classmate who offers unwavering emotional support and stays by her side through her darkest times.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Noor:</strong> Arsa's stepsister, whose jealousy and malice lead to the false allegations against Arsa and Tqi.</li>\r\n</ul><h2>Story Summary</h2><p>Sitara-e-Zeest follows Arsa, a top-performing student whose life takes a drastic turn when her jealous stepsister Noor frames her in a false scandal involving her chemistry teacher, Tqi. Believing the lies, Arsa's father beats her severely and cuts all ties with her. To save her from complete ruin, the college principal steps in, and Tqi agrees to a sudden nikah with Arsa to protect her from disgrace.</p><p>At first, their married life is filled with silence and emotional distance — Tqi remains reserved and serious, while Arsa battles low self-esteem, depression, and the fear of being a burden. Things begin to change when Tqi takes her to Islamabad to meet his family, where his elder sister welcomes her with unexpected warmth and motherly love, helping Arsa slowly heal.</p><p>Later, upon learning that Arsa is pregnant, Tqi finally opens up and confesses the admiration he had long kept hidden, clearing away every misunderstanding between them. The novel ends on a joyful note with the birth of their daughter, as both Arsa and Tqi fully embrace their love for each other.</p>",
