      "description": "<p><!--StartFragment--><!--EndFragment--></p><p><span>Read the complete Jalti Baarish novel online on our website or download the PDF to enjoy this powerful Urdu novel anytime, anywhere.</span></p><h2>Main Characters</h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Barrister Shahryar Mir Afridi:</strong> The male protagonist, a powerful and highly capable lawyer from the Afridi clan who is fiercely protective and deeply in love with his wife.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Farishtay Yousafzai (Farishtay Afridi):</strong> The female protagonist from the rival Yousafzai clan who marries Shahryar under intense family and tribal pressure.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Aaliyan Yousafzai:</strong> Farishtay's intersex sibling who faces cruel rejection from their family but finds unconditional love and protection from Zumarad Begum.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Banafshay Yousafzai:</strong> Farishtay's sister, who later marries Shahzeb Afridi.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Sajawal Choudhary:</strong> Shahryar's loyal friend and lawyer colleague who marries Malika.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Malika:</strong> Sajawal's cousin and eventual wife.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Shahir Afridi:</strong> Shahryar's lively cousin who marries Shehar Gul.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Shehar Gul:</strong> Shahir's cousin and eventual wife.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Zubair (Shahzeb) Afridi:</strong> Shahryar's cousin who marries Banafshay.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Marjaan Begum:</strong> Farishtay's mother — a deeply malicious and power-hungry woman driven by past rejections to commit horrific crimes against her own children.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Haqan Yousafzai &amp; Aalam Yousafzai:</strong> The ruthless elders of the Yousafzai clan, involved in illegal smuggling and the exploitation of their own family's women.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Zumarad Begum:</strong> An Afridi woman forced into a tribal marriage into the Yousafzai house years ago, who silently endures suffering while raising Aaliyan.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Habib Yousafzai:</strong> Farishtay's father, who eventually distances himself from his father and brother's crimes to seek justice.</li>\r\n</ul><h2>Story Summary</h2><p>Jalti Baarish is set against a dark, generation-spanning tribal enmity between the Afridi and Yousafzai clans. The scheming matriarch Marjaan Begum, along with her husband and father-in-law, forces Farishtay into a \"Vani\" — a tribal marriage meant to settle an old dispute — with Shahryar Mir Afridi, hoping to destroy his reputation and seize ancestral land. What they don't know is that Shahryar has long been investigating the Yousafzai family's dark crimes, and he willingly accepts the marriage to protect Farishtay from her toxic household, having secretly loved her all along.</p><p>The antagonists go to horrifying lengths to manipulate Farishtay — falsifying accusations against Shahryar, framing him for kidnapping, and even plotting to kill Farishtay's intersex sibling, Aaliyan, over misplaced \"honour.\" With sharp legal strategy and the help of loyal allies, Shahryar exposes the Yousafzai elders' criminal empire, and Farishtay finally learns the devastating truth about her mother's role in years of cruelty and deception. As the guilty are brought to justice, the extended family finds healing through love — culminating in several joyful weddings across the Afridi and Yousafzai households.</p>",
