      "description": "<p><!--StartFragment--><!--EndFragment--></p><p><span>Read the complete Qarh novel online on our website or download the PDF to enjoy this thrilling Urdu novel anytime, anywhere.</span></p><h2>Main Characters</h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Zin Kamal / Zin Alam Kaimal:</strong> The novel's central character, outwardly a successful hotel chain owner and hacker, but in reality an AD and later Deputy Director of the ISI.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Namal Kamal / Namal Bakhtawar Khan:</strong> A fearless and principled ASP police officer who is Zin's wife and always puts duty first.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Momin Murad:</strong> Zin's most loyal friend, known for his humor and witty banter.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Faiq Bakhtawar / FB:</strong> Namal's mischievous younger brother who helps with tech and computer work.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Jahangir Dilawar (JD) / Aamir bin Abdullah:</strong> A notorious international thief who is actually a Senior Undercover Officer from Malaysia.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Eish Mikhail:</strong> A self-obsessed and cunning thief/skimmer girl who later joins forces with Zin.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Sultan Alam:</strong> The elder prince of Sophia Mahal, government-loyal, who falls in love with Namal.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Fateh Alam:</strong> Sultan's younger brother, a famous singer who is intensely in love with Zin.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Aalam Faraz:</strong> Grandfather to Fateh, Sultan, and Zin — a well-known and arrogant politician.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Raisa Kamran Aalam:</strong> A cruel woman of Sophia Mahal consumed by vengeance and the desire for revenge.</li>\r\n</ul><h2>Story Summary</h2><p>Qarh is a mysterious, suspense-driven tale of enmity, duty, love, and sacrifice. The story begins in Lahore, where the strict and principled ASP Namal Kamal is posted, determined to rid the city of crime. Her path crosses with Zin Kamal — her husband of eight years, whom she believes to be nothing more than a hacker and a thief.</p><p>The story takes a dramatic turn when a Malaysian artist dies during an exhibition, and all evidence points to Zin. Bound by duty, Namal is forced to arrest him, and he is sentenced to death. But in reality, this is all part of a massive undercover ISI operation orchestrated by Zin himself, aimed at capturing the mastermind behind a diamond theft and human trafficking ring — Fateh Alam.</p><p>In Malaysia, JD and Eish Mikhail work to complete the mission. In the end, Zin returns alive and the truth comes to light. Raisa's jealousy and thirst for revenge end up destroying her own family — Sultan loses his life, and Raisa takes her own. The story concludes with forgiveness among loved ones and the healing of old wounds and regrets, true to its title, Qarh.</p>",
      "image": "images/149-6a7b0631b759f-qarh-novel-by-areej-rao-complete-pdf.webp",
