      "season_number": null,
      "description": "<h2><!--StartFragment--><!--EndFragment--></h2><p><span>Read the complete Kese Wafa Pe Yaqeen Kar Lain novel online on our website or download the PDF to enjoy this beautiful Urdu novel anytime, anywhere.</span></p><h2>Main Characters</h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Saleh Mansoor:</strong> The central protagonist, a biology teacher whose mother's abandonment left him deeply averse to marriage. He is highly principled, serious, and deeply religious.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ayat Mustafa (Ayat Saleh):</strong> The central female protagonist, a chemistry teacher who is innocent, cheerful, and talkative. She falls in love with Saleh after being moved by his character and his beautiful Quran recitation.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Maaz Siddiqui:</strong> Saleh's cousin and Ayat's paternal cousin, who initially has feelings for Ayat but honours his family's wishes and marries his other cousin, Wajeeha, eventually falling deeply in love with her.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Wajeeha Hamdani (Jiya):</strong> Maaz's cousin and later his wife — a sociology student passionate about painting, who has loved Maaz since childhood.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Saleha Begum:</strong> Saleh's mother, who abandoned her devoted husband years ago for a wealthy man, shattering the family, and later returns seeking forgiveness after fleeing an abusive second marriage.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Junaid Kazmi:</strong> Saleh's childhood best friend and a psychiatrist who helps him cope with his trauma — lively, humorous, and fiercely loyal.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Anaya:</strong> Ayat's beloved 8-year-old sister, who becomes close friends with Saleh and calls him \"Big Brother.\"</li>\r\n</ul><h2>Story Summary</h2><p>Kese Wafa Pe Yaqeen Kar Lain follows Saleh Mansoor, whose childhood was shattered when his mother abandoned his father for a wealthy man, leaving him deeply distrustful of women and firmly opposed to marriage. Everything changes when he meets Ayat Mustafa, a fellow teacher who is captivated by his piety after hearing his Quran recitation. When Saleh saves her from an accident, his guarded heart begins to soften, and the two are eventually united in marriage — with Ayat asking, as her dowry, that Saleh personally teach her Quran recitation.</p><p>Alongside their story runs the gentle romance of Saleh's cousin Maaz, who lets go of his feelings for Ayat and comes to deeply love his own cousin, Wajeeha, whom he marries. Meanwhile, Saleh's estranged mother returns to Pakistan broken and remorseful, revealing the pain and betrayal she suffered after leaving her family. Choosing mercy over resentment, Saleh and his siblings forgive her and welcome her back into the family.</p><p>Through Ayat's healing love, Saleh slowly lets go of his old wounds. Years later, after completing their studies abroad, Saleh and Ayat return to Pakistan to live a peaceful life with their daughter, surrounded by a family finally made whole again.</p>",
      "image": "images/151-6a7c562ec3f07-kese-wafa-pe-yaqeen-kar-lain-novel-by-esha-afzal-complete.webp",
