      "description": "<p><span>Read the complete Aisi Ki Taisi novel online on our website or download the PDF to enjoy this entertaining Urdu novel anytime, anywhere.</span></p><h2>Main Characters</h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Chahat &amp; Braq:</strong> Chahat is a carefree girl deeply in love with her first cousin, Braq — a serious businessman who is initially strict and distant but eventually marries and falls for her.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Ana &amp; Danyal:</strong> Next-door neighbours who constantly bicker and trade insults, despite their mothers' rivalry, and eventually fall in love and marry.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Minahil &amp; Areesh (Major Balaj Sikander):</strong> Minahil is an arrogant, wealthy, headstrong girl. Areesh appears to be a quiet, bespectacled student — but is actually Major Balaj Sikander, a secret army agent on an anti-smuggling mission.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Sheela Beebe &amp; Faisal:</strong> The elderly grandparents of Ana and Danyal, who share a humorous, late-in-life rooftop romance their grandchildren constantly spy on.</li>\r\n</ul><h2>Story Summary</h2><p>Aisi Ki Taisi is a lively tale of family drama, neighbourhood rivalries, and hidden identities. It opens with the comedic bickering of two neighbouring families — Ana and Danyal can't stand each other, while their mothers compete over petty social rivalries. Meanwhile, their grandparents secretly flirt from their rooftops, and Chahat pines hopelessly for her distant cousin Braq.</p><p>Things take a dramatic turn when Minahil, an arrogant girl, is left stranded at the altar by her fiancé and is hastily married off to Areesh, a quiet student, to save her family's honor. At the same time, Braq's original bride goes missing, and Chahat steps in to marry him instead. The story then reveals a massive twist: Areesh, along with two other seemingly unrelated men, is actually the same person — Major Balaj Sikander, an undercover army agent infiltrating a dangerous human trafficking ring using multiple disguises.</p><p>As Balaj carries out a daring military operation to dismantle the trafficking network and rescue dozens of girls, he survives near-fatal danger and returns to a transformed Minahil, who has fallen in love with his true self. Braq comes to fully trust and cherish Chahat, while Danyal and Ana finally marry too — alongside their grandparents, who tie the knot in a joyful double wedding. Years later, the whole family lives happily together, their children carrying on the same playful traditions.</p>",
