      "description": "<h2><!--StartFragment--><!--EndFragment--></h2><p><span>Read the complete Jaam-e-Mohabbat novel online on our website or download the PDF to enjoy this powerful Urdu novel anytime, anywhere.</span></p><h2>Main Characters</h2><ul>\r\n<li><strong>Zoya Shah:</strong> The innocent, orphaned female protagonist who faces severe hardship, mistreatment, and kidnapping due to her greedy aunt.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Balaj Mir:</strong> A brave, noble police officer who rescues Zoya and becomes her shield and support.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Azaan Sikander:</strong> A handsome businessman and Balaj's close friend.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Amaan Sikander:</strong> Azaan's intelligent and reserved brother, who falls in love with Noor.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Noor Mustaqeem:</strong> A hardworking girl who joins Amaan's company as an employee.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Nudrat (Chachi):</strong> Zoya's cruel, greedy aunt who plots against her for financial gain.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Waseem:</strong> The villainous gangster involved in Zoya's kidnapping.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Shaista &amp; Haseeb:</strong> Nudrat's children, whose poor choices and bad company lead to their own downfall.</li>\r\n</ul><h3>Story Summary</h3><p>Jaam-e-Mohabbat follows Zoya, an innocent orphaned girl who suffers greatly at the hands of her abusive aunt, Nudrat. Driven by greed, Nudrat conspires with the criminal Waseem to have Zoya kidnapped, leaving her held captive under brutal conditions — yet she remains remarkably resilient through it all.</p><p>Her rescue comes in the form of Balaj Mir, a dedicated police officer whose investigation leads him straight to Waseem's hideout just in time to save Zoya from harm. He brings her to safety, nurses her back to health, and vows to protect her while working to bring her tormentors to justice.</p><p>Alongside their story runs a gentler romance between Amaan Sikander and Noor, a humble girl who joins his company and slowly wins his heart. Meanwhile, karma catches up with the greedy Nudrat as her own children fall into bad company and ruin. Blending crime, vengeance, and healing romance, the novel closes with justice served and love triumphing over cruelty.</p>",
